# ── Gemini ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-side ONLY. Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that would ship the key to
# the browser and let kids (or anyone) bypass the safety gate.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ── Google transport: AI Studio vs Vertex AI (owner ask 2026-08-12) ──────────
# Which Google backend serves EVERY Gemini call — generation and the safety
# classifier alike (src/lib/google-backend.ts). Flip it and flip it back at
# will; models, safetySettings, thinking budgets and the fallback chain are
# identical on both. This is a transport switch, nothing else.
#   studio  (default, unset) → AI Studio, reads GEMINI_API_KEY
#   vertex                   → Vertex AI EXPRESS mode, reads VERTEX_API_KEY
# An unrecognised value fails closed at boot rather than silently serving
# Studio while you believe you cut over.
# GEMINI_BACKEND=vertex
#
# Vertex express key — a DIFFERENT credential from GEMINI_API_KEY, on a
# different (GCP) billing account. Vertex never borrows the Studio key: a
# silent fallback would 401 mid-turn instead of failing with a clear message.
# VERTEX_API_KEY=
#
# After flipping, PROVE it before anyone opens the app (global rule 12):
#   npm run check:backend                       # whatever .env selects
#   GEMINI_BACKEND=vertex npm run check:backend # force the Vertex path
# NOTE: Vertex bills through GCP, not the AI Studio key — the Sparks cost
# reconciliation still reads AI Studio prices (platform TECH_DEBT).

# Model used for the kid-facing conversation.
# 2026-08-18 owner decision: moved to the Gemini 3.6/3.7 line. 3.6-flash is
# $0.75/$3.75 per M vs 3.5-flash's $1.50/$9.00, so a build turn costs ~57% less
# and the kid is debited ~57% fewer Sparks for the same game. Must exist in
# MODEL_CATALOG (src/lib/model-registry.ts) — an uncatalogued id still RUNS but
# bills at the unknown-model fallback rate and drops to the legacy ladder.
GEMINI_CHAT_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash

# Fast/cheap model used for the red-flag safety classifier.
GEMINI_SAFETY_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-lite

# Game-BUILD turns only (middle-path thinking, 2026-07-09): bounded reasoning
# budget + extra output headroom so games match gemini.google.com quality on
# the same model. Ordinary chat is unaffected (thinking stays 0 for instant
# replies). Defaults shown; junk/empty values fall back to them.
# Fallback chain for Gemini 503/429 spikes and model deprecations
# (BUG-FIX-LOG 2026-07-11, PRD-MODEL-FALLBACK): when the primary refuses with
# a capacity error (or its id is retired), we walk this chain — one attempt
# per model — instead of erroring at the kid. Up to 4, comma-separated.
# Default: gemini-3.7-flash,gemini-3.5-flash,gemini-3.1-pro-preview,gemini-3.5-flash-lite
# GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODELS=gemini-3.7-flash,gemini-3.5-flash,gemini-3.1-pro-preview,gemini-3.5-flash-lite
# GEMINI_BUILDER_THINKING_BUDGET=1024
# GEMINI_BUILDER_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=24576

# ── Cross-provider fallback (owner decision 2026-07-20) ──────────────────────
# src/lib/model-registry.ts routes a failed turn to the CHEAPEST model of the
# SAME capability tier, crossing providers freely — quality tier first, price
# within the tier. A provider with no key here is dropped when the chain is
# built, so a failover never discovers a missing key mid-incident.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=      # Claude (prompt-only — see gate below)
# MOONSHOT_API_KEY=       # Kimi   (prompt-only + China data-handling — see below)
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=       # DeepSeek (prompt-only + China data-handling — see below)
#
# Optional base-URL overrides (self-host / regional endpoint / test proxy):
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages
# MOONSHOT_BASE_URL=https://api.moonshot.ai/v1
# DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/v1
#
# Pin the chain order explicitly instead of price-sorting (ids must exist in
# MODEL_CATALOG; unknown ids are dropped, never forwarded to an SDK):
#
# ⚠ REQUIRED for the 2026-08-18 ladder. The primary (gemini-3.6-flash) is a
# WORKHORSE-tier model, and the automatic rule refuses to escalate to a richer,
# pricier tier mid-incident (PRD-MODEL-FALLBACK §4 — that is how a 503 becomes
# a bill shock). So without this pin the frontier rescues 3.7-flash and
# 3.1-pro-preview are simply never tried. Pinning is the documented deliberate
# exception; the price climb is the point, and it only ever fires on a
# Google-side outage.
MODEL_FALLBACK_CHAIN=gemini-3.7-flash,gemini-3.5-flash,gemini-3.1-pro-preview,gemini-3.5-flash-lite
#
# ⚠ CHILD-SAFETY GATE — read before setting. Ari's posture (CLAUDE.md §3) is
# input rules → PROVIDER-ENFORCED safety thresholds → child-safety prompt.
# Gemini enforces per-request thresholds (safetySettings); OpenAI is fronted by
# a moderation pass (openai-generation.ts) so its models are `provider-enforced`.
# Anthropic (Claude), Moonshot (Kimi) and DeepSeek have NEITHER — they are
# `prompt-only` and EXCLUDED from every chain unless this flag is exactly "1"
# AND their key is set. Setting it removes the middle safety layer for those
# models. Do not set it in production without an explicit posture decision.
# Verify the model ids + prices in MODEL_CATALOG and run the prompt-portability
# eval first.
# ALLOW_PROMPT_ONLY_SAFETY_MODELS=1
#
# ⚠ DATA HANDLING — Moonshot (Kimi) AND DeepSeek are China-based providers.
# Sending a child's prompts there is a privacy/compliance decision; keep
# MOONSHOT_API_KEY / DEEPSEEK_API_KEY unset until that review, independent of
# the safety flag above.
#
# Prove a provider key works before trusting it in a chain (global rule 12):
#   npm run check:backend -- --provider deepseek

# Self-healing preview (docs/FEATURES.md + platform PRD-SELF-HEALING-PREVIEW):
# set to 0 to run INSTRUMENT-ONLY — probes + preview_verify telemetry still
# fire, but broken games are never auto-repaired (no extra Gemini calls).
# Default (unset/anything else) = repair ON, max 2 attempts, 20s bail.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PREVIEW_REPAIR=0

# ── Kid hints / next-ask chips (docs/2026-07-27_PRD_KidHintsAndNextBestAsk.md,
# implemented 2026-07-28) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# On a build OR edit turn, the model appends 3 contextual "what to try next"
# ideas (2 concrete + 1 imaginative "what if") via a trailing sentinel line,
# parsed server-side and never shown raw to the kid. Edit turns use their own
# prompt variant (one line after the last >>>>>>> REPLACE) — verified inert
# against the patch pipeline by unit tests + a live A/B on patch compliance.
# Any parse failure falls back to a static "change this game" pool. Adds a few
# output tokens per turn only when ON — the prompt section itself is gated, so
# cost is exactly zero when OFF. Server-side only; the client never reads this
# var directly, it just renders chips when the server sends them.
# Default OFF. Set to exactly "1" to enable (any other value = off).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ENABLE_KID_HINTS=1

# ── Community Help (docs/PRD-COMMUNITY-HELP.md Phase 1) ──────────────────────
# The 🆘 tab on the game preview: a stuck child files a picture-reason ticket
# that a grown-up answers from /admin/help. The reply is one-way (👍 / 😕 only)
# and every reply is mirrored into the parent's alerts.
#
# Turning this on CREATES AN OBLIGATION: once a child can ask a person for
# help, someone has to be there. The promise the copy makes is "by tomorrow"
# (a 16h target — see src/lib/help-sla.ts), so don't enable it during a week
# nobody is watching the queue. Reply from /admin/help with ADMIN_SECRET.
# Default OFF. Set to exactly "1" to enable (any other value = off).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ENABLE_HELP_BUTTON=1
#
# The PROACTIVE nudge ("Stuck on this one? A grown-up can take a look") after
# the repair loop gives up or three asks change nothing. Separately flagged
# because it's the change most likely to spike ticket volume onto one person —
# enable it only once the queue's real volume is known. Requires the button
# flag above; on its own it does nothing. Thresholds: src/lib/stuck-signal.ts.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ENABLE_HELP_NUDGE=1

# The 🎤 Idea mic tab over the preview (docs/PRD-IDEA-BUTTON.md) — one tap to
# speak an idea straight into the build queue, no typing, no chat detour.
# Owner decision 2026-07-31 (OFF) REVERSED 2026-08-01 — reinstated with the
# same functionality; the kill switch stays in the code (src/lib/idea-mic.ts's
# ideaMicEnabled()) in case it needs to flip off again. Set to exactly "1" to
# enable (any other value = off). This is a NEXT_PUBLIC_* var — it must be
# present in the real .env at BUILD time to inline into the client bundle;
# setting it after a build has already run has no effect until the next build.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ENABLE_IDEA_MIC=1

# ── Authentication (Ariantra SSO) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# kidgemini no longer runs its own OAuth. Login happens once on the platform
# (studio.ariantra.com/login — Google OR username/password); the platform sets
# the `ariantra_session` cookie on .ariantra.com and this app verifies it.
#
# AUTH_JWT_SECRET: MUST be the SAME value as the Ariantra-Platform app's
# AUTH_JWT_SECRET (the two apps share the session signature). Server-only.
# Rotating it requires redeploying BOTH apps together. Also the x-admin-secret
# every server-to-server bridge route checks (parent-pin-otp, sparks, and —
# 2026-07-28, Feature 5 admin consolidation — /api/admin/usage-bridge, which
# Platform's /studio/admin "Usage & Cost" tab calls into).
AUTH_JWT_SECRET=
# Cookie domain the logout route clears (defaults: prod '.ariantra.com', dev host-only).
# SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN=.ariantra.com
# Where the sign-in buttons send users (default shown; override for local dev).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ARIANTRA_LOGIN_URL=https://studio.ariantra.com/login
# Platform base for the server-to-server publish bridge (default shown).
# LOCAL DEV: set this to your local platform, or every "Put it in the Arcade"
# goes to PRODUCTION and is rejected (dev secret ≠ prod secret) — the publish
# fails with a "check the setup" error (BUG-FIX-LOG 2026-07-11).
# ARIANTRA_API_BASE=https://studio.ariantra.com
# ARIANTRA_API_BASE=http://localhost:3000   # ← local dev

# ── Operator / parent controls ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The parent PIN is NO LONGER an env var: each family sets a 4-digit PIN on
# their own account (/parent — stored hashed in SQLite parent_auth).
# ADMIN_SECRET gates the /admin usage dashboard (operator-only). No fallback:
# unset means /admin is OFF. Use a long random string.
ADMIN_SECRET=

# USD→INR rate for the /admin dashboard's ₹ figures. NOT a live FX feed —
# update it when the rate moves; unset falls back to the default in
# src/lib/pricing.config.ts. Stored costs stay USD; ₹ derives at read time.
USD_INR_RATE=

# ── Observability ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-request model-decision ledger (owner ask 2026-07-21): one JSON line per
# request recording every model call made (primary/hedge/fallback/backup, with
# timing + outcome) and which won — the piece usage_events (winner-only) and
# app.log (fallback lines only) can't give. Unset → <project>/logs/model-decisions.jsonl.
# 10MB cap, rotates to <path>.1 (mirrors LOG_FILE / app.log).
# MODEL_LEDGER_FILE=

# Where the SQLite database file lives (alerts, settings, transcripts).
DATABASE_PATH=./data/kidgemini.db

# ── Payments (Razorpay) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One-time payment flow (Orders + Checkout). KEY_ID is publishable (the server hands it to the
# browser for Checkout); KEY_SECRET and WEBHOOK_SECRET are server-only — never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#   Dashboard → Settings → API Keys  (use Test keys in dev, Live keys in prod)
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
# Webhook signing secret. Dashboard → Settings → Webhooks → add endpoint:
#   https://kidgemini.ariantra.com/api/billing/webhook   (events: payment.captured, order.paid)
# The value below must match the "secret" you set on that webhook.
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Game-edit patch mode ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Follow-up requests on an existing game are answered with a minimal
# SEARCH/REPLACE patch (untouched parts survive byte-for-byte), with a strict
# hunks-only retry when the model tries to rewrite the whole file.
# Set to "off" to restore exact pre-patch behavior (full regeneration on every
# follow-up, as before 2026-07-18). Any other value (or unset) = enabled.
GAME_EDIT_PATCH=
